<description>
Straighten a colored snake path into a single-column strip preserving pixel order.

Input structure:
- bg = most common color.
- Non-bg pixels form a single 4-connected path (snake) with exactly two endpoints.
- Each path pixel may be a different non-bg color.

Rule:
- Find the two endpoints (cells with only one path neighbor) of the snake.
- Begin at the top-left-most endpoint and trace the path cell by cell.
- Output an (N×1) column listing each cell's color in traversal order.

Key insight: The path is a simple chain with no branches; choosing the top-left-most endpoint fixes a unique reading direction.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "snake-shaped polychrome sprite",
  "transform": "stretch vertically into a line",
  "grid_shape": "tight crop"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  task: Straighten a colored snake path into a single-column strip preserving pixel order
  grid: 16x16 [observed]
  background: any single ARC color; most-frequent color in grid
  snake:
    structure: single 4-connected path (no branches), exactly 2 endpoints, no 2x2 blocks
    total_pixels: 20-30
    color_segments: 3-6 contiguous runs of distinct non-bg colors along path; colors may repeat across non-adjacent segments
    segment_length: 2-9 pixels each
    non_bg_colors: 3-5 distinct colors
    shape: staircase of alternating horizontal/vertical straight runs (lengths 1-5 each); 7-11 turns total
    vertical_direction: mostly downward; occasional upward allowed (test_0 has one) [observed]
    horizontal_direction: left or right, varies per segment
    placement: does not touch grid border (margin >= 1 on all sides)
    path_span: covers 60-90% of grid rows within bounding box
  output: Nx1 column listing each path pixel's color in traversal order (start from top-left-most endpoint)

generation_strategy:
  approach: build snake path directly, then place on grid
  steps:
    1. Choose grid 16x16, pick bg color, pick 3-5 distinct non-bg colors
    2. Build snake as a staircase path on the grid starting from a random interior cell near top-left
    3. Alternate between vertical runs (1-5 cells, mostly downward) and horizontal runs (1-5 cells, left or right), ensuring path stays within grid with margin >= 1
    4. Continue until total path length reaches 20-30 pixels, with 7-11 turns
    5. Assign colors to path in contiguous segments of length 2-9, choosing from the non-bg palette; 3-6 segments total matching total path length
    6. Verify no 2x2 filled blocks exist (reject and retry the problematic turn if so)
    7. Place path pixels on bg-filled grid; derive output by tracing from top-left-most endpoint
```
</generation_spec>
